IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 4531 of 2022
CITATION: (2010) 9 SCC 218
YEAR: 2010

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: G.S. Singhvi, A.K. Ganguly

PARTIES:
Arun Kumar Agrawal vs National Insurance

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Motor Vehicles Act, 1988

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 166 Motor Vehicles Act, Section 168 Motor Vehicles Act

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
gratuitous domestic labor, loss of dependency, gender dignity

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Affirmed that the contribution of a deceased homemaker is invaluable and must be properly recognized in motor accident awards rather than dismissed on bare technicalities.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 166 Motor Vehicles Act, Section 168 Motor Vehicles Act.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

